.TH REPO-SQUEEZE 1 "May 2026" "repo-squeeze" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
repo-squeeze \- squeeze a local repository into an LLM-friendly digest
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B repo-squeeze
.RI [ path ]
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B ingest
.RI [ path ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B repo-squeeze
turns a local repository or folder into a single text digest suitable for pasting into a large language model. The output contains a summary, a tree-style directory view, and the contents of each included file separated by path headers.
.PP
By default the digest is copied to the system clipboard with
.BR clipboardy (1).
The default target is the current working directory. Only local paths are supported.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help text and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show the package version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Print debug information to stderr while files are processed.
.TP
.BR \-L ", " \-\-list\-templates
List the available exclusion templates.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " "\-\-output \fR[\fIfile\fR]"
Write the digest to a file. If
.I file
is omitted, writes
.B digest.txt
in the current directory.
.TP
.BR \-S ", " \-\-stdout
Write the full digest to standard output and do not print status text.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-no\-clipboard
Skip every digest output target and print only the summary.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " "\-\-include \fIpatterns...\fR"
Include only files matching one or more glob patterns. Directories are still traversed to find matches.
.TP
.BR \-e ", " "\-\-exclude \fIpatterns...\fR"
Exclude files or directories matching the given patterns. Repeated, space-separated, and comma-separated forms are accepted.
.TP
.BR \-T ", " "\-\-template \fIname\fR"
Apply an exclusion template on top of the built-in defaults. Available templates include
.BR typescript ", " bun ", " docs ", " go ", " hono ", " nextjs ", " node ", " python ", " react ", " rust ", and " vite .
The alias
.B \-\-exclude\-template
is also accepted.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-include\-dangerous
Include paths that are excluded by the built-in safety defaults, such as
.B node_modules
and
.BR .git .
.TP
.BR \-g ", " \-\-include\-gitignored
Skip loading patterns from
.B .gitignore
and
.B .gitingestignore
files.
.TP
.BR \-F ", " "\-\-ignore\-file \fIfile\fR"
Also load ignore patterns from this additional ignore file name, for example
.BR .customignore .
.TP
.BR \-s ", " "\-\-max\-size \fIbytes\fR"
Maximum size of one file to include. Default:
.BR 10485760 .
.TP
.B \-\-include\-pdf
Extract text from PDF files using
.B unpdf
and include the result in the digest.
.TP
.B \-\-include\-env
Include
.B .env
files that are otherwise excluded by built-in defaults and templates.
.TP
.BR \-N ", " \-\-line\-numbers
Prefix each line of file content with a right-padded line number, separated by
.RB \(dq " | " \(dq.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Print the tree and the list of files (with sizes) that would be included, without reading file contents or producing a digest. Useful for previewing what an ingest run would capture.
.TP
.B \-\-ipynb
Convert
.B .ipynb
(Jupyter Notebook) files to a readable text format that includes cell sources, execution counts, and text outputs. Without this flag,
.B .ipynb
files are included as raw JSON.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " "\-\-repo \fIurl\fR"
Clone the remote Git repository at
.I url
to a temporary directory, squeeze it to a digest, and then delete the temporary directory. Accepts URLs such as
.B https://github.com/torvalds/linux
or
.BR https://github.com/torvalds/linux.git .
.SH OUTPUT FORMAT
The digest is composed of three sections, joined with blank lines:
.IP \(bu 2
A
.B summary
with directory name, resolved path, file count, and excluded directories.
.IP \(bu 2
A
.B tree
in
.BR tree (1)
style.
.IP \(bu 2
.B File sections
separated by headers of the form
.BR "FILE: relative/path" ,
each followed by the file contents.
.SH MATCHING RULES
.B repo-squeeze
supports glob-style include and exclude patterns such as
.BR *.ts ,
.BR src/**/*.ts ,
and
.BR .next/ .
By default it applies built-in exclude patterns for common generated, dependency, cache, binary, and version control paths, plus patterns from
.B .gitignore
and
.BR .gitingestignore .
Use
.B \-\-include\-gitignored
to skip ignore-file loading,
.B \-\-include\-dangerous
to override built-in safety defaults, and
.B \-\-include\-env
to allow
.B .env
files through.
.SH EXAMPLES
Copy a digest of the current directory to the clipboard:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
repo\-squeeze
.fi
.RE
.PP
Write a digest to
.B digest.txt
in the current directory:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
repo\-squeeze \-o
.fi
.RE
.PP
Stream the digest to standard output and pipe it elsewhere:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
repo\-squeeze \-\-stdout | pbcopy
.fi
.RE
.PP
Limit the digest to TypeScript sources and apply the
.B typescript
template:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
repo\-squeeze \-i "src/**/*.ts" README.md \-T typescript
.fi
.RE
.PP
Preview what would be included without producing a digest:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
repo\-squeeze \-\-dry\-run
.fi
.RE
.PP
Include
.B .env
files and prefix each line with its line number:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
repo\-squeeze \-\-include\-env \-\-line\-numbers
.fi
.RE
.PP
Convert Jupyter notebooks to readable text instead of raw JSON:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
repo\-squeeze \-\-ipynb
.fi
.RE
.PP
Clone and squeeze a remote repository:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
repo\-squeeze \-r https://github.com/torvalds/linux.git
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B repo-squeeze
exits with status
.B 0
on success and
.B 1
on any error during argument parsing or ingestion.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1),
.BR tree (1),
.BR pbcopy (1),
.BR xclip (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Written for the
.B repo-squeeze
project. See the project README for licensing and contribution information.
